Description: include the byte-order helper by its bare kit name
 FFont.cpp used the full-path form <os/support/ByteOrder.h>. V\OS's
 default include path covers every kit directory, and the bare name is
 what the port rules mandate; the full-path form also tripped the
 build-tree wrapper headers/build/os/support/ByteOrder.h:1, which
 re-included itself through build/config_headers (first -I) until the
 include-depth limit.
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/FontBoy
--- a/src/alien/FFont/FFont.cpp
+++ b/src/alien/FFont/FFont.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifndef _BYTEORDER_H
-#include <os/support/ByteOrder.h>
+#include <ByteOrder.h>
 #endif
 
 #include <netinet/in.h>
